        "id": 1010050
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T23:37:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "but they do have to get rid of the outMediaTypes array themselves, right? That is:\n\n```C++\n   size_t n \u003d AMediaCodecStore_countSupportedMediaTypes();\n   auto *supportedTypes \u003d new AMediaCodecSupportedMediaType[n];\n   media_status_t err;\n   err \u003d AMediaCodecStore_getSupportedMediaTypes(\u0026supportedTypes, n);\n   ...\n   \u003cuse supportedTypes\u003e\n   ...\n   // not OK\n   delete(supportedTypes[0]);\n   \n   // Probably also bad?\n   delete[](supportedTypes);\n   \n   // Necessary\n   delete(supportedTypes);\n```\n\nThat\u0027s a bit foot-gunny to me, but I assume there\u0027s a reason we can\u0027t just provide them the array too?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 59,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "13f68784890cada31e25488087b59f9864c492d5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
