      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T23:37:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this keeping state inside the method somewhere? Is it thread-safe? (ie, like `strtok` / `strtok_r`)",
      "revId": "13f68784890cada31e25488087b59f9864c492d5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d195f0f3_38c4b219",
        "filename": "media/ndk/include/media/NdkMediaCodecStore.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 1021605
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-08T22:30:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that we don\u0027t want to do that. Instead, we should make this required. E.g. If called with a different format while .... the behavior is undefined.\n\nIn all fairness, we will just loop from the outCodecInfo in the implementation through our linear array of codec infos and use the current format.",
      "parentUuid": "6f5c09c4_38548918",
      "revId": "13f68784890cada31e25488087b59f9864c492d5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "31254797_96d47e6a",
        "filename": "media/ndk/include/media/NdkMediaCodecStore.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010050
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-09T00:27:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not sure I follow - make which part required?  Just want to avoid having a situation where two threads querying codec info will clobber each other.",
      "parentUuid": "d195f0f3_38c4b219",
      "revId": "13f68784890cada31e25488087b59f9864c492d5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f062e7d_1dcb6f3b",
        "filename": "media/ndk/include/media/NdkMediaCodecStore.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 1021605
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-11T23:53:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t want to keep thread-local state in these APIs. It\u0027s required to use the same format for successive iterations, otherwise the behavior is undefined.",
      "parentUuid": "31254797_96d47e6a",
      "revId": "13f68784890cada31e25488087b59f9864c492d5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
