      "key": {
        "uuid": "f4b169ef_5b3decfd",
        "filename": "media/ndk/include/media/NdkMediaCodecStore.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 82,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010050
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T23:37:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Stylistically, the APEX Codec API Wonsik is adding has a different way to iterate, requiring an incrementing index to be passed in until you get a null result.\n\nCould we use a consistent pattern for this kind of \u0027interate over all entries\u0027 method, or are there reasons each API needs to stick with what they have?\n\nNot that an index is all that pretty, but it at least seems to avoid storing any state in the method.",
      "revId": "13f68784890cada31e25488087b59f9864c492d5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9286b50c_d9395bb6",
        "filename": "media/ndk/include/media/NdkMediaCodecStore.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 82,
      "author": {
        "id": 1895465
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-08T22:13:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@lajos@google.com How do you think about it?",
      "parentUuid": "f4b169ef_5b3decfd",
      "revId": "13f68784890cada31e25488087b59f9864c492d5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1997d364_fac6a5f2",
        "filename": "media/ndk/include/media/NdkMediaCodecStore.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 82,
      "author": {
        "id": 1021605
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-08T22:30:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue is that using an index will create an extra call (getInfoAtIndex) and restricts our implementation to actually using a vector-like construct with an index. Here we could use a linked list.\n\nAPEX Codec API is used to iterate throw all codecs, and not just for codecs that support a specific media type. What we found that nearly 99% of apps just want to find a codec for a format, and they make mistakes because they try to implement that themselves (usually incorrectly), hence this proposed API.",
      "parentUuid": "9286b50c_d9395bb6",
      "revId": "13f68784890cada31e25488087b59f9864c492d5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d2480aaa_74885e8a",
        "filename": "media/ndk/include/media/NdkMediaCodecStore.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 82,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010050
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-09T00:27:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Technically we could count nodes in a linked list, but agree that would be inefficient to start at root each time instead of a fixed offset / follow the next pointer.\n\nSo soudns reasonable to me to have this be different.",
      "parentUuid": "1997d364_fac6a5f2",
      "revId": "13f68784890cada31e25488087b59f9864c492d5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "813b86bb_d13a18ca",
        "filename": "media/ndk/include/media/NdkMediaCodecStore.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 108,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010050
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T23:37:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "where does the set of names available come from?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 108,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 108,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "13f68784890cada31e25488087b59f9864c492d5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5fd91a35_1d9531e7",
        "filename": "media/ndk/include/media/NdkMediaCodecStore.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 108,
      "author": {
        "id": 1021605
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-08T22:30:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is for cases when you already know the codec name, e.g. in MediaCodec itself although for now we are not implementing this on top of the NDK. Many times application code gets the codec name (from the findDecoder/Encoder methods above), and keeps only the codec name, which is guaranteed to uniquely identify the codec and its info.\n\nPerhaps we need to say that?",
      "parentUuid": "813b86bb_d13a18ca",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 108,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 108,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "13f68784890cada31e25488087b59f9864c492d5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "31de7489_8328d5dc",
        "filename": "media/ndk/include/media/NdkMediaCodecStore.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 108,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010050
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-09T00:27:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027d be good to mention the options, at least as breadcrumbs for developers to know where to look for names.",
      "parentUuid": "5fd91a35_1d9531e7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 108,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 108,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "13f68784890cada31e25488087b59f9864c492d5",
